            <div xml:id="d79-a2">

                <pb facs="0231" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg97"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 751.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wingfield to Mr.
                            Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States at San José, Costa
                            Rica</hi></placeName><lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-10-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 25,
                    1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 12th
                    October, 1887, I understand that the contract between the Costa Rican Government
                    and the Spanish American Line of steamers, by which a rebate of 5 per centum on
                    duties upon merchandise brought upon said steamers is allowed, is being carried
                    out.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Rich’d
                            Wingfield.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
